7.3.s:
Saddhābalaṁ vīriyañca,
hirī ottappiyaṁ balaṁ;
Satibalaṁ samādhi ca,
paññā ve sattamaṁ balaṁ;
Etehi balavā bhikkhu,
sukhaṁ jīvati paṇḍito.

7.4.s:
Saddhābalaṁ vīriyañca,
hirī ottappiyaṁ balaṁ;
Satibalaṁ samādhi ca,
paññā ve sattamaṁ balaṁ;
Etehi balavā bhikkhu,
sukhaṁ jīvati paṇḍito.

7.33.e:
One respectful of the Teacher and the teaching,
keenly respecting the Saṅgha;
respecting immersion, being energetic,
and keenly respecting the training;

7.37.s:
Yamhi etāni ṭhānāni,
saṁvijjantīdha puggale;
So mitto mittakāmena,
atthakāmānukampato;
Api nāsiyamānena,
bhajitabbo tathāvidho”ti.

7.62.s:
Passa puññānaṁ vipākaṁ,
Kusalānaṁ sukhesino;
Mettaṁ cittaṁ vibhāvetvā,
Satta vassāni bhikkhavo;
Sattasaṁvaṭṭavivaṭṭakappe,
Nayimaṁ lokaṁ punāgamiṁ.

7.64.e:
An angry person slays their father;
their mother, too, they slay.
An angry person slays a saint;
a normal person, too, they slay.
